cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the research software or reproducibility materials in this repository, please cite this archived release."
title: "FALCON Yemen 2020: BGP Research Software and Reproducibility Archive"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Ezzaldeen
    family-names: Al-Tayar
    affiliation: "Faculty of Engineering and Information Technology, Taiz University, Taiz, Yemen"
repository-code: "https://github.com/EZZALDEEN049/falcon-yemen-resilience"
abstract: "Versioned research software and supporting reproducibility materials for network-specific BGP routing observations surrounding Yemen's January 2020 FALCON submarine-cable disruption. The repository includes a reviewed evidence package, historical non-event reference comparisons, and methodological limitations."
keywords:
  - BGP
  - RIPE RIS
  - Internet measurement
  - submarine-cable disruption
  - Yemen
  - research reproducibility
